WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.502
-Our next guest is a talented
actress you know

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:04.236
from films such
as "In the Heights"

00:00:04.236 --> 00:00:05.471
and the Scream franchise.

00:00:05.471 --> 00:00:08.074
She stars in the latest
installment, "Scream VI."

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:09.175
It should be
in theaters everywhere

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:11.243
this Friday, March 10th.
Let's take a look.

00:00:11.243 --> 00:00:13.880
[ Suspenseful music plays ]
[ Thudding ]

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:14.847
-Hey!

00:00:14.847 --> 00:00:16.850
[ Vehicle horns blaring ]

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:19.619
Don't worry.
I got you.

00:00:22.154 --> 00:00:23.890
-Are you kidding me?
-You have a better idea?

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:24.957
[ Thudding ]
-No.

00:00:24.957 --> 00:00:31.230 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:32.432
[ Thudding ]
-Come on.

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:33.699
Eyes on me.

00:00:33.699 --> 00:00:34.667
Keep your eyes on me.

00:00:35.135 --> 00:00:36.236
-Go!
[ Thudding ]

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:39.605
-[ Sobbing ]
-Oh, my God.

00:00:39.605 --> 00:00:41.140
-I got you.
I got you.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:44.077
[ Thudding ]
-[ Grunts ]

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:46.145
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.145 --> 00:00:48.514
-Please welcome to the show
Melissa Barrera, everybody.

00:00:48.514 --> 00:00:50.516
[ Band plays mellow funk ]
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:50.516 --> 00:01:08.167 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:09.936
Welcome!
I'm so happy to have you here!

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:12.872
-I'm so happy. This is my first
late night show ever.

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:15.407
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Well, you're doing a great job.

00:01:15.407 --> 00:01:16.776
[ Whistling ]
Usually --

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:18.878
Usually, first timers
just wander off

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:20.379
and you made it right over here.

00:01:20.379 --> 00:01:23.182
-Well, so far, I didn't trip,
which was what I was afraid of.

00:01:23.182 --> 00:01:24.918
-I remember the first time
I was on a talk show,

00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:26.652
that was my biggest concern,
was just like

00:01:26.652 --> 00:01:28.420
making it fully
to the couch okay.

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:30.089
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah. So, so far, so good.
-You're off to a great start.

00:01:30.089 --> 00:01:31.324
Off and running.
-Thanks.

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:32.625
-Congratulations on the movie.

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:35.227
I know you had the premiere here
and was it fantastic?

00:01:35.227 --> 00:01:36.862
-It was incredible.
It was last night

00:01:36.862 --> 00:01:41.000
at the Lincoln Center AMC
and it was so magical.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.870
We didn't get a premiere for the
last one because, you know,

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:45.672
Omicron.
-Right, right.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.672 --> 00:01:48.675
-And so this was like
a double whammy premiere

00:01:48.675 --> 00:01:51.543
and it felt big and it was
wonderful and magical.

00:01:51.543 --> 00:01:53.346
-And, you know, I've lived
in the city for, you know,

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:54.447
over 20 years and I will say,

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:55.815
when a big horror movie
comes out,

00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:58.117
there is no more fun place
to see it than Times Square.

00:01:58.117 --> 00:02:00.886
[ Laughter ]
I mean that genuinely,
like those crowds

00:02:00.886 --> 00:02:03.489
are exactly the kind of crowds
that have the sort of fun

00:02:03.489 --> 00:02:05.357
that you're supposed
to have at movies like this.

00:02:05.357 --> 00:02:09.229
-I mean, horror is such a like
a communal experience.

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:12.198
You need to see it with people
because people are shouting

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:14.733
and yelling at the screen
and gasping

00:02:14.733 --> 00:02:17.003
and it's contagious
and it's fun to do that.

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:19.071
-This is you
with some of your costars.

00:02:19.071 --> 00:02:21.173
You all look wonderful,
but this is even more exciting.

00:02:21.173 --> 00:02:25.244
This is your family joined you
and they were all there.

00:02:25.244 --> 00:02:27.380
And were they so proud?
Were they so happy?

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:32.051
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Yeah. That's my sister Rossana;
my mom;

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:34.554
my husband;
and my baby sister, Mayela.

00:02:34.554 --> 00:02:36.021
And my other sister, Regina,

00:02:36.021 --> 00:02:37.289
who lives in Spain,
couldn't be here.

00:02:37.289 --> 00:02:39.592
But to me,
the most important thing

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:41.594
is sharing my work
with my family,

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:44.229
so, the fact that they all
made it out was really special.

00:02:44.229 --> 00:02:46.265
-Now, of course, anybody
who's watching a "Scream" movie

00:02:46.265 --> 00:02:47.800
is trying to guess
who is Ghostface,

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:48.968
who's behind the mask.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.536
Your family,
did they participate in that?

00:02:50.536 --> 00:02:51.904
Were they trying
to figure it out?

00:02:51.904 --> 00:02:54.107
They do, because I don't
tell them anything.
-Really?

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:55.108
Do they try
to get it out of you

00:02:55.108 --> 00:02:56.409
or they know
that it's pointless?

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:57.743
-Every day, they try.
-Okay, gotcha.

00:02:57.743 --> 00:03:01.013
[ Laughter ]
They try to like catch me
off-guard.

00:03:01.013 --> 00:03:02.748
But I don't --

00:03:02.748 --> 00:03:05.651
I am really bad
when I start oversharing,

00:03:05.651 --> 00:03:07.920
so, I just say
I'm not going to tell anyone.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:12.925
And that means not even my mom,
not my husband, not anyone, so.

00:03:12.925 --> 00:03:15.428
They get to participate
in the whodunit mystery

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:18.430
and they get to --
And I love watching them

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:20.299
watch the movie
for the first time

00:03:20.299 --> 00:03:24.470
and they're like real reactions
and it's really -- it's cool.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.539
-That's good. And did any
of them correctly guess?

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:28.307
Did they admit
to you afterwards?
-No, they did not, yeah.

00:03:28.307 --> 00:03:29.442
-Alright. That's even more fun.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:30.643
[ Laughter ]
It is fun.

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:32.979
-There is a scene,
a fantastic scene --

00:03:32.979 --> 00:03:34.446
This movie takes place
in New York City,

00:03:34.446 --> 00:03:36.048
which is a first
for the Scream franchise.

00:03:36.048 --> 00:03:38.450
There's this very scary scene
that takes place on the subway.

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:41.687
-I really apologize
to all subway users

00:03:41.687 --> 00:03:42.955
[ Laughter ]
in New York City.

00:03:42.955 --> 00:03:45.391
-Now, I will say
it's bad enough,

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:46.759
even without the slashers...

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:48.127
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:50.062
-...like without Ghostface,
like it wasn't like people

00:03:50.062 --> 00:03:52.665
were like, "Oh, the subways were
great until that."

00:03:52.665 --> 00:03:54.566
[ Laughter ]
-I know.

00:03:54.566 --> 00:03:57.270
-But was it fun to shoot it here
in New York

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:58.470
and to bring the franchise here?

00:03:58.470 --> 00:03:59.905
-We did shoot in New York.

00:03:59.905 --> 00:04:01.907
-Well, that is heartbreaking.

00:04:01.907 --> 00:04:03.676
[ Laughter ]
-I know.
-I guess that makes sense.

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:05.043
I didn't see Ghostface
running around.

00:04:05.043 --> 00:04:07.113
[ Laughter ]
-I know.
Well, have you seen him like

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:09.882
standing on corners creepily
as part of like the marketing?

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:11.584
-That's not okay, by the way.
-I know!

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:12.952
[ Laughter ]
I know it's not!
-Yeah.

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:15.554
-I actually am not sure
if it's part of the marketing

00:04:15.554 --> 00:04:18.724
or if it's just someone decided
to do that and made the news.

00:04:18.724 --> 00:04:20.059
-Like there's
a Times Square Elmo,

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:21.828
but that's not "Sesame Street."
-Yeah.

00:04:21.828 --> 00:04:24.230
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:26.832
-That's not a reminder
to tune in.

00:04:26.832 --> 00:04:29.535
-But they built --
So, in Mont--

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:31.037
We shot in Montreal.

00:04:31.037 --> 00:04:33.239
They had a whole soundstage

00:04:33.239 --> 00:04:36.875
and they built a subway
with a station

00:04:36.875 --> 00:04:39.145
and the train would go in
and out of the station,

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:41.513
inside a studio.
It was mind-blowing.

00:04:41.513 --> 00:04:43.048
And it was dirty, too.

00:04:43.048 --> 00:04:45.450
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:46.852
-Very accurate.

00:04:46.852 --> 00:04:49.455
[ Laughter ]
-Now, I remember

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:52.191
when I saw the first "Scream"
movie in theaters --

00:04:52.191 --> 00:04:54.527
I know I'm older than you --
I Googled it.

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:55.661
That's how I know. I didn't --

00:04:55.661 --> 00:04:57.129
[ Laughter ]
Like at first, I was like,

00:04:57.129 --> 00:04:58.664
"Are we the same age?"
But no.

00:04:58.664 --> 00:05:01.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:04.370
So, I'm assuming you did not see
the first one in theaters,

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.806
but you must've seen --
remember the first time

00:05:06.806 --> 00:05:08.340
you saw the "Scream" movie.
-I do remember.

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:11.177
I didn't see it when it came out
because I was six, but I --

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:14.046
[ Laughter ]
-Don't. It's not important
how old you are.

00:05:14.046 --> 00:05:16.248
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.248 --> 00:05:18.317
-I did -- I was obsessed
with horror movies

00:05:18.317 --> 00:05:21.353
when I was like 10, 11, 12.

00:05:21.353 --> 00:05:23.389
And I wasn't allowed
to watch horror movies,

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:26.058
so, I would either lock myself
in my room

00:05:26.058 --> 00:05:28.961
or, at sleepovers
with my friends,

00:05:28.961 --> 00:05:32.698
watch "Scream"
and "Final Destination"

00:05:32.698 --> 00:05:34.199
and, you know, "I Know What You
Did Last Summer"

00:05:34.199 --> 00:05:36.469
and all those obsessively.

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:38.270
I'm kind of a masochist that way

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:41.174
[ Laughter ]
because I love
watching horror movies

00:05:41.174 --> 00:05:42.841
and I cannot sleep at night,

00:05:42.841 --> 00:05:45.344
but I kind of love that,
weirdly, yes.

00:05:45.344 --> 00:05:48.014
-Do you remember the first one
that really scared you,

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:49.781
was it one of the --
-Yes, "Chucky."

00:05:49.781 --> 00:05:51.383
[ Laughter ]
-"Chucky," yeah.

00:05:51.383 --> 00:05:52.518
-Yeah.
-"Chucky's" not okay,
either, yeah.

00:05:52.518 --> 00:05:55.120
[ Laughter ]
-It was not okay.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:57.790
I specifically remember
this scene where he's --

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:00.526
It's like a back --
the back of like a big like

00:06:00.526 --> 00:06:02.661
moving truck or something
and he's --

00:06:02.661 --> 00:06:06.999
like the little doll
is holding someone hostage --

00:06:06.999 --> 00:06:09.067
however that happens --
[ Laughter ]

00:06:09.067 --> 00:06:12.037
and someone's following in a car
or running or something

00:06:12.037 --> 00:06:14.240
and the little doll
just flips them off.

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:15.174
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.174 --> 00:06:16.709
And it's actually hilarious,

00:06:16.709 --> 00:06:18.444
but it was so scary
to me at the time.

00:06:18.444 --> 00:06:22.081
[ Laughter ]
-I like that,
of all of Chucky's crimes,

00:06:22.081 --> 00:06:24.182
-I know!
-the one you couldn't stand for
is rudeness.

00:06:24.182 --> 00:06:26.685
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:26.685 --> 00:06:28.987
-That's what I remember.

00:06:28.987 --> 00:06:31.390
-I think that says
you're a very polite person.

00:06:31.390 --> 00:06:34.326
Of the many things we should
take away, it's that.

00:06:34.326 --> 00:06:35.761
Hey, congratulations
on the movie.

00:06:35.761 --> 00:06:37.162
It was so delightful
to have you here.

00:06:37.162 --> 00:06:38.731
You're a pro.
Let me just tell you,
-Thank you.

00:06:38.731 --> 00:06:40.065
Thank you so much.
-You're a pro at being
a talk show guest.

00:06:40.065 --> 00:06:42.000
[ Cheering and applause ]
Melissa Barrera, everybody.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.237
"Scream VI" will be in theaters
everywhere this Friday.

00:06:44.237 --> 00:06:45.905
We'll be right back
with Margaret Atwood.

